{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788291494,"nonce":"YXiH4nv5uAlwYypw7V6ar3TXxVc=","message":"CLOSED by session 19, branch `spec/until-condition` (commit df3e0b4), proven\nlive. `Source/AutoRimmer/Materials.cs` is the new file.\n\n## THE ISSUE'S OWN CASE, BEFORE AND AFTER, FROM RAW ENVELOPES\n\nBoth are dry runs of the same 5x7 bedroom, `*=WoodLog`, on a quicktest map with\nNO stockpile zone and 300 loose unforbidden WoodLog. Banked under\n`accept/runs/s19-20260901/envelopes/`.\n\n    acc1adc737-005  (old code, a leftover from an earlier suite run)\n      materials  [{\"def\":\"WoodLog\",\"count\":185,\"in_stockpiles\":0}]\n      shortfall  [{\"def\":\"WoodLog\",\"needed\":185,\"in_stockpiles\":0,\"short_by\":185}]\n\n    accfc287ba-039  (this round)\n      materials  [{\"def\":\"WoodLog\",\"count\":185,\"available\":300,\"in_stockpiles\":0,\n                   \"availability_basis\":\"reachable-unforbidden-by-a-colonist\"}]\n      shortfall  []\n\nThat is the last acceptance bullet — \"re-run of the M2 bedroom placement: bill\n185 WoodLog, `shortfall[]` empty, room still built\" — and the room WAS still\nbuilt: `advance {until:{layout:\"ly-5\"}}` finished it 10,255 ticks later,\n`role: \"Bedroom\"`, `proper: true`.\n\n## Acceptance, item by item\n\n- **\"loose on unzoned ground and reachable -\u003e EMPTY shortfall, both counts\n  distinguishable\"** — above, and check 2.5c asserts the two numbers DIFFER,\n  which is the whole finding rather than a coincidence of the fixture.\n- **\"present but FORBIDDEN -\u003e non-empty and says so\"** — check 2.3, STAGED\n  rather than observed (the suite forbids the wood itself, so the case does not\n  depend on how the map arrived):\n\n      shortfall [{\"def\":\"WoodLog\",\"needed\":185,\"short_by\":185,\"available\":0,\n                  \"in_stockpiles\":0,\"forbidden\":300,\n                  \"hint\":\"there is enough of this on the map, but 300 of it is\n                          FORBIDDEN — `unforbid` is the fix, not mining\"}]\n\n- **\"same for material that exists but is unreachable\"** — the bucket EXISTS\n  (`Availability.Unreachable`, with its own hint naming a door or a wall rather\n  than a shortage) and it NEVER FIRED on any of the four bench runs, because\n  none of them staged a walled-off stack. Not claimed as proven; filed as part\n  of `039e359` with an acceptance criterion of its own.\n- **\"genuinely no material -\u003e `short_by` equals the full bill\"** — check 2.6,\n  a bedroom stuffed with `Plasteel` on a map with none: `available: 0`,\n  `short_by == needed`, hint \"genuinely short: nothing else of this def is on\n  the map within reach\", and NEITHER `forbidden` NOR `unreachable` present\n  (2.6e) — presence is the signal, so the three problems never blur.\n- **\"`construction`'s `missing[]` answers consistently\"** — they call the same\n  routine now (`Materials.Of` through `ConstructionVerbs.MissingRows`), so they\n  cannot disagree; 2.7d asserts it anyway on the live layout. Sample:\n  `{\"def\":\"WoodLog\",\"count\":185,\"available\":300,\"in_stockpiles\":0,...}` with\n  `short_by` ABSENT, which is the news.\n- **\"cites its vanilla provenance the way `Blockers.cs` does\"** — every envelope\n  carrying a bill or a `missing[]` also carries `materials_basis`:\n\n      gate  \"RimWorld/WorkGiver_ConstructDeliverResources.ResourceValidator\"\n\n  asserted verbatim by check 2.2g, with `builders` (how many colonists were\n  asked) beside it. `Materials.cs`'s header cites five members by name:\n  `ResourceDeliverJobFor`, `ResourceValidator`, `MaxPathDanger`,\n  `PawnCanAutomaticallyHaulFast`, and records the grep — `SlotGroup`,\n  `slotGroup`, `haulDestination`, `Stockpile` and `resourceCounter` appear\n  NOWHERE in that work giver.\n- **\"does not re-enter a lazy getter per element; a per-element map scan is a\n  cost note\"** — the builder snapshot is taken ONCE per bill, not once per def\n  (`FreeColonistsSpawned` clears and rebuilds its cached list on every access,\n  DigestVerb hazard 1). Stacks are capped at 200 per def and reported when the\n  cap bites. `Reachability.CanReach` fills a `ReachabilityCache` — an observer\n  write, named in the file and given the same ruling `CostListCalculator`'s\n  cache and `DangerWatcher.dangerRatingInt` already got: idempotent, RNG-free,\n  never scribed, filled by the game itself on every haul job.\n- **Zero red errors** across the whole 140-check run.\n\n## What is deliberately NOT reproduced, and named in the file rather than hidden\n\n- `p.CanReserve(t, …)`. A stack somebody is already hauling is reserved, and\n  calling that \"missing\" would be exactly the wrong answer — the material is on\n  its way. It is also per-tick churn, and a bill is not a job.\n- The `UnfinishedThing`/`BoundBill` clause: an unfinished thing is not a\n  construction material.\n- The socially-proper clause: it fires only for human-edible ingestibles and no\n  building is made of those.\n- `GenClosest`'s 9999-cell radius and `FindAvailableNearbyResources`' 5-cell\n  widening. Both are about WHICH stack a pawn walks to, not whether one exists.\n\n`th.Fogged()` and `th.IsBurning()` ARE reproduced and get their own buckets.\n\n## `DigestVerb.resources` was checked and left alone, as the issue asked\n\nIt publishes `scope: \"stockpiles-only\"` and draws no conclusion, so it is honest\nas it stands. Its FIELD DOCS now name `Materials.Of` as the count a verdict must\ncome from, and the header's own warning — \"any wave-3 build verb that gates on a\nresource count must say 'in stockpiles' or count things itself\" — is annotated\nwith the date it came true.","files":null}]}